# Lines tools/qemu-test must see, in this order, as whole serial lines.
# In QEMU: the virtio-net driver PD finds the card, reads
# its MAC address and sets up its queues; net_client gives it every receive
# buffer, five descriptors it must drop and count, and an ARP request for
# QEMU's gateway; the gateway's reply comes back through the driver.
NOWAYOS: virtio-net: starting
NOWAYOS: virtio-net: ready on transport 7, MAC 52:54:00:12:34:56
NOWAYOS: net-client: starting: 10.0.2.15 at 52:54:00:12:34:56
NOWAYOS: net-client: sent 4 malformed descriptors, an ARP request (who has 10.0.2.2? tell 10.0.2.15) and the request's buffer again: 6 descriptors
NOWAYOS: virtio-net: dropped so far: 0 oversize frames, 0 malformed frames, 5 bad descriptors, 0 corrupt queue indices, 0 bad used entries
NOWAYOS: net-client: 10.0.2.2 is at 52:55:0a:00:02:02

# Output that fails the test at once if it appears anywhere (substring match):
# a fault reported by the Microkit monitor, a kernel error message, a panic,
# or a PD giving up.
!MON|ERROR
!seL4(CPU
!panicked
!gave up
!queue:
